STATUS

Create a new visual concept for the Green Frontier chapter finale's mobile
siege boss. This replaces Thorncrown's character concept; it does not change
the boss encounter, balance, or gameplay behavior.

REFERENCE INPUTS

- Attach the first frame of the Ancient War Oak idle sequence,
  `android-app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/anim_boss_ancient_war_oak_idle_000.png`,
  as the primary style reference. Match its painterly rendering, shape
  definition, material texture, lighting, and level of detail. Borrow only the
  art style; do not copy its tree-like character design, face, branches, or
  silhouette.
- Attach `assets_src/bosses/thorncrown.png` only as a technical reference for
  the existing boss sprite's 1145 × 1374 canvas, transparent margins, game
  camera, scale, and ground baseline. Do not retain Thorncrown's humanoid body,
  wooden antler crown, leafy cape, armor, or bow.
- The new creature is a Green Frontier mobile siege boss. Keep its silhouette
  readable at match scale and facing toward the BLUE fortress.

PROMPT

Create one full-body, grotesque fantasy siege-snail boss sprite for Urkaaaz.
The boss is a huge land snail carrying an ancient, partially collapsed stone
watchtower as its shell. It should feel like a living siege engine that has
slowly absorbed a ruin, not a normal snail with a miniature building simply
placed on its back.

Give it a low, heavy, muscular gastropod body with thick folds, a wide mouth,
and two long, uneven eye stalks. Make the face grotesque and expressive:
bulging mismatched eyes, one drooping and one staring, a crooked sneer, and a
few large irregular blunt teeth. Keep the expression strange and memorable,
with dark-comic personality rather than a noble or solemn expression. Avoid
gore, exposed flesh, or horror-body imagery.

Build the shell from massive, weathered gray-brown masonry shaped like a broken
watchtower or gatehouse fragment. Give it a strong, readable arched silhouette,
one or two broken battlement peaks, and a few missing or offset stones.
Integrate roots, moss, vines, and grass naturally into the cracks so the ruin
belongs to the Green Frontier. Add only restrained warm bronze details, if
needed. The shell must remain the dominant, unmistakable feature and should
suggest that the creature can ram a fortress gate.

Show the snail in a stable three-quarter view facing left toward the BLUE
fortress, with its head and eyestalks clearly visible in front of the shell.
Keep the pose imposing and mobile, but not humanoid. The body rests low on the
ground baseline; the ruin shell rises high enough to occupy roughly the same
vertical space as the existing boss sprite. Keep the face, shell silhouette,
mouth, and eyes readable after the sprite is scaled down in the match.

Use the Ancient War Oak frame as the rendering-style guide while giving the
snail its own restrained Green Frontier palette: stone gray, damp earth brown,
moss and leaf greens, with small warm bronze accents. Match the reference's
painterly shape definition and material finish, not its character design or
exact color placement. The snail should feel grotesque, weathered, and
slightly absurd, yet still credible as the chapter's final mobile siege
threat.

Render only the complete boss sprite. Do not draw the battlefield, scenery,
ground plane, cast shadow, impact effect, slime trail, health bar, HUD, name,
text, or any other character. Keep all visual elements attached to the snail
or its integrated ruin shell so the game can composite the sprite directly
into the battlefield.

TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS

- Output exactly one PNG named `green_frontier_siege_snail_concept.png`.
- Canvas: exactly 1145 × 1374 pixels, portrait, RGBA.
- Use genuine alpha transparency outside the full creature. Do not use a
  checkerboard, matte, flat-color background, or opaque glow.
- Keep the complete shell, eye stalks, body, and foot inside the canvas with a
  small transparent safety margin. Preserve a clear, stable bottom baseline.
- Match the original boss sprite's camera, approximate scale, and overall
  visual footprint so a later runtime replacement can be reviewed without
  changing the presentation contract.
- Save the review image to `assets_src/bosses/green_frontier_siege_snail_concept.png`.
  Do not overwrite or delete `assets_src/bosses/thorncrown.png`.
- This is one static concept still. Do not create animation frames, variants,
  a sprite sheet, a contact sheet, or a battle scene.

